# Deliberately excluded, and it must stay that way. The README's "fast
# incremental rebuild" recipe copies _build/prod/rel/axon into an existing
# image, which only works if the host that built the release has a glibc no
# newer than the image's. It does not here: releases built on this Fedora
# host link against GLIBC_2.38, the Complement image is Debian bookworm
# (glibc 2.36), and the copied beam.smp dies on startup with
#   beam.smp: /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6: version `GLIBC_2.38' not found
# Every homeserver container then fails to boot and the whole Complement run
# hangs instead of failing loudly. Build the image with
#   docker build -f complement/Dockerfile -t axon-complement:latest .
# which compiles the release inside the image and cannot skew.
_build/
deps/
.git/
.github/
.elixir_ls/
*.log
erl_crash.dump
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
e2e-client/node_modules/
e2e-client/test-results/
e2e-client/playwright-report/
